      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by expressing the three integers in terms of their remainders when divided by 24. Let the three integers be \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). According to the problem, we have:\n\\[ a \\equiv 10 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\\[ b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\\[ c \\equiv 12 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\nThis means that we can write:\n\\[ a = 24k + 10 \\]\n\\[ b = 24m + 4 \\]\n\\[ c = 24n + 12 \\]\nfor some integers \\(k\\), \\(m\\), and \\(n\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the sum of these three integers:\n\\[ a + b + c = (24k + 10) + (24m + 4) + (24n + 12) \\]\n\\[ a + b + c = 24k + 24m + 24n + 10 + 4 + 12 \\]\n\\[ a + b + c = 24(k + m + n) + 26 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24. We can rewrite the expression as:\n\\[ a + b + c \\equiv 26 \\pmod{24} \\]\nSince \\(26 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{24}\\), we have:\n\\[ a + b + c \\equiv 2 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the three integers is divided by 24 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
